From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 05:13:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ActivityThread: load the old-app layer for 32-bit apps below
 API 14

Games written for Dalvik, which kept direct object pointers for a
32-bit application with targetSdkVersion below 14, do not start on ART:
they read a Java byte[] through its object pointer, leak local
references and assume a heap below 2 GiB. The product ships a library
that gives such an application's native code those behaviours
(device/kernarium/andarium/oldapp). Load it into the process of a
32-bit application that targets below API 14, in handleBindApplication
next to the other legacy-application handling and before any code of
the application can run, and into no other process. A failed load is
logged and the application starts as before.
---
 core/java/android/app/ActivityThread.java | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/core/java/android/app/ActivityThread.java b/core/java/android/app/ActivityThread.java
index b7d9f653023e91bc8c9145f0f6bf3014f921503c..d798332ffbc817da39797790ffc18150947bbc36 100644
--- a/core/java/android/app/ActivityThread.java
+++ b/core/java/android/app/ActivityThread.java
@@ -8048,6 +8048,20 @@ public final class ActivityThread extends ClientTransactionHandler
             AsyncTask.setDefaultExecutor(AsyncTask.THREAD_POOL_EXECUTOR);
         }
 
+        // An application written for Dalvik (a 32-bit one that targets below API 14) reads a
+        // Java byte[] through its object pointer, leaks local references and assumes a heap
+        // below 2 GiB. This library gives its native code what Dalvik gave it; nothing else
+        // in the process changes, and no other application maps it. It is loaded before any
+        // code of the application can run.
+        if (!Process.is64Bit()
+                && data.appInfo.targetSdkVersion < Build.VERSION_CODES.ICE_CREAM_SANDWICH) {
+            try {
+                System.load("/system/lib/libkernarium_oldapp.so");
+            } catch (Throwable t) {
+                Slog.w(TAG, "kernarium: old-application layer not loaded", t);
+            }
+        }
+
         // Let the util.*Array classes maintain "undefined" for apps targeting Pie or earlier.
         UtilConfig.setThrowExceptionForUpperArrayOutOfBounds(
                 data.appInfo.targetSdkVersion >= Build.VERSION_CODES.Q);
